// REJECTS: no viable alternative at input '{'bsonType''
//
// A `jsonSchema:` body written with SINGLE quotes. MongoDBSchemaLexerGrammar imports
// M3LexerGrammar and then declares its OWN `QUOTED_STRING` on DOUBLE quotes, because the
// schema body is literal JSON handed to Jackson -- so in this section, and nowhere else in
// Legend, `"..."` is the string form and `'...'` is not a string at all.
//
// Every other grammar in the corpus is the other way round: M3's STRING is single-quoted and
// a double quote is invalid. A rewrite with one shared string lexer -- or one that treats the
// two quote characters as interchangeable, which is what a hand-written lexer does by default
// and what most languages do -- accepts this file and then hands Jackson something it cannot
// read.
//
// The single-quote convention also governs collection names and `include` paths in this
// section: ../fixtures/t2-mongodb.pure writes `Collection "firm-data"`, double-quoted.
###MongoDB
Database fixture::neg::SingleQuotedSchema
(
  Collection Person
  (
    jsonSchema: {
      'bsonType': 'object',
      'properties': {}
    };
  )
)
